# Day 22 – Introduction to Git: Your First Repository

## 🎯 Objective

Today I practiced the basics of Git by creating a local repository, configuring Git, creating a Git commands reference, staging and committing changes, and viewing commit history.

---

# 1. Git Installation & Configuration

| Task               | Command                                                   | Purpose                   |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| Check Git version  | `git --version`                                           | Verify Git installation   |
| Configure username | `git config --global user.name "Aarti"`                   | Set Git username          |
| Configure email    | `git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"` | Set commit email          |
| View configuration | `git config --list`                                       | Display Git configuration |

### Example

```bash
git --version

git config --global user.name "Aarti"

git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"

git config --list
```

> **Note:** Replace `your-email@example.com` with the email you actually use for your Git/GitHub account.

