# 3. Understanding `.git/`

| Command   | Purpose                       |
| --------- | ----------------------------- |
| `ls -a`   | Show hidden files/directories |
| `cd .git` | Enter Git metadata directory  |
| `ls`      | View `.git` contents          |
| `cd ..`   | Return to project directory   |

### Important Concept

When you run:

```bash
git init
```

Git creates a hidden:

```text
.git/
```

directory.

The `.git/` directory contains Git's internal repository information and metadata.

```text
devops-git-practice/
│
├── git-commands.md
│
└── .git/
    ├── HEAD
    ├── config
    ├── objects/
    ├── refs/
    └── ...
```

