# 14. `.git/` Directory

| Concept    | Explanation                                                            |
| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Created by | `git init`                                                             |
| Name       | `.git`                                                                 |
| Type       | Hidden directory                                                       |
| Contains   | Git internal information and metadata                                  |
| Purpose    | Allows Git to manage repository history                                |
| If deleted | Local Git repository history/configuration is lost from that directory |

### Important

```bash
git init
```

creates:

```text
.git/
```

Do **not** normally modify or delete files inside `.git/` manually.

