# 17. Git Interview Quick Revision

| Question                          | Short Answer                                                        |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| What is Git?                      | A distributed version control system used to track changes in files |
| What does `git init` do?          | Initializes a directory as a Git repository                         |
| What is `.git`?                   | Directory containing Git's internal repository metadata             |
| What does `git status` do?        | Shows the current state of the working directory and staging area   |
| What does `git add` do?           | Moves selected changes into the staging area                        |
| What does `git commit` do?        | Saves staged changes as a commit                                    |
| What is the staging area?         | A place where changes are selected before committing                |
| What does `git log` do?           | Displays commit history                                             |
| What does `git log --oneline` do? | Displays compact commit history                                     |
| What is a commit?                 | A recorded snapshot of staged changes                               |
| Why use commit messages?          | To describe what changed in a commit                                |

